Z||000018||pherder||09-03-2001||08:59 PM||||Songman (and others),<P>That dash (the EURO) was originally built by Auto Designs out of San Diego, CA and is sold by PISA (amoung others.)<P>I had one in my 308 kit built by the original builders and they covered it in EXTREMELY nice leather.  Cost me ~$4000 about 5 years ago (included the door panels in leather and molded carpeting.)<P>ONE thing I <B>DID'T</B> like about it was the position of the instrutments ... they are too high in the dash!  Look at where the stock Fiero instrutments are ... low and around the steering column.  These are up ~3-5" higher so the steering wheel rim covers the top of the speedo and the tach!  Makes seeing what you speed you are driving on the highway and where the tach is interesting.<P>I reversed the location of the radio and the top instrutments in the center pod.  That way I could get a tape into the sterio!<P>Plus the gated shifter was a <B>PAIN</B> to shift into third or fourth and forget shifting fast ... it ain't going to go!<P>It did look good inside the 308 ... fooled a lot of people with that dash inside.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/308_Interior.jpg"> <P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000019||Pontiaddict||09-04-2001||12:58 AM||||I'd be happy if someone made a new instrument cluster pod and radio pod that fit into the stock dash, maybe make them 1 piece like the wraparound dash, but not wrapped around so much because that thing makes me claustrophobic. (Though not as much as the Knight Rider dash.)||||reg||1
Z||000020||FieroGTguy||09-04-2001||11:06 AM||||Well, my favorite dash has to be the one I have.  Most people know who I bought it from.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And since I love car audio, more space, and digital gauges...  It is the one for me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry, but it is a one of a kind.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/pages/dash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/pages/dash.html</A> <P>Greg<BR>||||reg||1
